## System Architecture

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[Therapeutic Scheduler] -->|Trigger Alarm| B[Behavioral FSM]
    B -->|State: Prompting| C[Haptic & Audio Cues]
    B -->|State: Recording| D[Audio Input Pipeline]
    D -->|PCM Stream| E[Custom Ring Buffer]
    E -->|Write File| F[Encrypted SQLite Storage]
    B -->|State: CBT Labeling| G[Metadata Tagging]
```

### The Scheduler Pipeline
The core scheduler maintains a priority queue of upcoming alarms. It uses OS-level wait conditions (`std.Thread.Condition`) to sleep efficiently, waking up only when an alarm fires or when the queue is modified.

### Low-Latency Audio Pipeline
Audio callbacks run on high-priority system threads where heap allocations are strictly forbidden to prevent dropouts:
```mermaid
graph LR
    PCM[Hardware PCM Input] --> Callback[Audio Callback Thread]
    Callback -->|Zero-Alloc Writes| RingBuf[Fixed Sized Ring Buffer]
    RingBuf -->|Low Priority Thread| Encoder[Opus Encoder / Disk Writer]
```

